- [L1] LSC1 failed: Every guard must be satisfiable under the declared ranges of its referenced variables. | Guard `v1 = 'Abort'` on `b1 -> n5` cannot be evaluated: `v1` has no declared range. | Guard `v2 = 'Provide userdata'` on `b2 -> n7` cannot be evaluated: `v2` has no declared range. | Guard `v3 = 'Abort'` on `b3 -> n9` cannot be evaluated: `v3` has no declared range. | DSL: guard(b1,n5,"v1 = 'Abort'"); guard(b2,n7,"v2 = 'Provide userdata'"); guard(b3,n9,"v3 = 'Abort'")
- [L2] LSC3 failed: Guards outgoing from XOR/OR branches must cover the whole evaluated state space. | Branch `b1` cannot be evaluated: `v1` has no declared range. | Branch `b2` cannot be evaluated: `v2` has no declared range. | Branch `b3` cannot be evaluated: `v3` has no declared range.
